<% content_for :title, "Input" %>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Forms</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Input</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    The control a <%= link_to "Field", field_path, class: "text-primary underline" %> renders by default. In a form,
    <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">Ui::FieldComponent.new(model: @user, attribute: :email)</code> gives you this input already named, valued,
    labelled and marked invalid from the record, so you rarely render it yourself. On its own it is a native
    <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">&lt;input&gt;</code> drawn from the design tokens, with one option of its own, <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">size:</code>, the control
    scale it shares with Button, Select and Textarea.
  </p>
</div>

<%# Preview %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
<div id="input-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background flex flex-wrap items-start gap-6 p-12 mb-8">
  <div class="grid gap-2 w-56">
    <%= render(Ui::LabelComponent.new(for: "default-input", class: "text-xs font-mono text-muted-foreground")) { "default" } %>
    <%= render Ui::InputComponent.new(id: "default-input", name: "default", value: "Jane Cooper") %>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-2 w-56">
    <%= render(Ui::LabelComponent.new(for: "placeholder-input", class: "text-xs font-mono text-muted-foreground")) { "placeholder" } %>
    <%= render Ui::InputComponent.new(id: "placeholder-input", name: "placeholder", placeholder: "you@example.com") %>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-2 w-56">
    <%= render(Ui::LabelComponent.new(for: "focused-input", class: "text-xs font-mono text-muted-foreground")) { "focus (tab to me)" } %>
    <%= render Ui::InputComponent.new(id: "focused-input", name: "focused", value: "Tab to me") %>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-2 w-56">
    <%= render(Ui::LabelComponent.new(for: "invalid-input", class: "text-xs font-mono text-muted-foreground")) { "invalid" } %>
    <%= render Ui::InputComponent.new(id: "invalid-input", name: "invalid", value: "not-an-email", aria: { invalid: true }) %>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-2 w-56">
    <%= render(Ui::LabelComponent.new(for: "disabled-input", class: "text-xs font-mono text-muted-foreground")) { "disabled" } %>
    <%= render Ui::InputComponent.new(id: "disabled-input", name: "disabled", value: "Can't touch this", disabled: true) %>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-2 w-56">
    <%= render(Ui::LabelComponent.new(for: "password-input", class: "text-xs font-mono text-muted-foreground")) { "type: password" } %>
    <%= render Ui::InputComponent.new(type: "password", id: "password-input", name: "password", value: "hunter2") %>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-2 w-56">
    <%= render(Ui::LabelComponent.new(for: "sm-input", class: "text-xs font-mono text-muted-foreground")) { "size: :sm" } %>
    <%= render Ui::InputComponent.new(size: :sm, id: "sm-input", name: "sm", value: "Jane Cooper") %>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-2 w-56">
    <%= render(Ui::LabelComponent.new(for: "lg-input", class: "text-xs font-mono text-muted-foreground")) { "size: :lg" } %>
    <%= render Ui::InputComponent.new(size: :lg, id: "lg-input", name: "lg", value: "Jane Cooper") %>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-8">
  Tab to the "focused" field to see the focus ring — an offset outline drawn from the
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">--ring</code> token, the same idiom Button uses.
</p>

<%# Usage %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-border mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-muted px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#input-usage" class="text-xs text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-card px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="input-usage" class="text-card-foreground"><%= h(example_input_usage) %></code></pre>
</div>

<%# Options %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Options</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Name</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Type</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Default</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["type",         "String",  '"text"', "The input type attribute — text, email, password, and so on."],
        ["size",         "Symbol",  ":default", "One of :sm, :default, :lg — the heights Button's sizes have, so controls at one size line up. The kit's scale, not the HTML size attribute."],
        ["class",        "String",  "nil",    "Merged over the default classes with tailwind_merge — the caller always wins."],
        ["aria-invalid", "Boolean", "nil",    "Set aria: { invalid: true } to draw the invalid boundary and focus colour. In a Field, the Field sets it from the errors."],
        ["disabled",     "Boolean", "nil",    "Forwarded straight to the native disabled attribute."],
        ["…",            "Any",     "—",      "Every other keyword (id:, name:, value:, placeholder:, data:, aria:, …) is forwarded to the root element."],
      ].each do |name, type, default, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= name %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= type %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><%= default %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# Accessibility %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Accessibility</h2>
<ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2 mb-8 list-disc ps-5">
  <li>Invalid is <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-invalid</code>, not a class: a screen reader hears it, and the red boundary is drawn from it.
      A Field sets it, and points <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-describedby</code> at the error.</li>
  <li>The boundary comes from <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">--input</code>, never the fill, so it keeps 3:1 against whatever surface the input
      sits on — transparent in light mode, a translucent <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">--muted</code> tint in dark.</li>
  <li>The focus ring is an offset outline from <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">--ring</code>, visible in forced-colors mode.</li>
  <li>An input needs a name a screen reader can read: a Field's label, or <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria: { label: }</code> when there's
      no visible one.</li>
</ul>

<%# Not this %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">When not to use it</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-8">
  A labelled field in a form is a <%= link_to "Field", field_path, class: "text-primary underline" %>, which renders this for you.
  A choice from a known list is a <%= link_to "Select", select_path, class: "text-primary underline" %> or
  <%= link_to "Choices", choices_path, class: "text-primary underline" %>, not free text; more than a line is a
  <%= link_to "Textarea", textarea_path, class: "text-primary underline" %>. A checkbox or radio is Choices, not an input with a type.
</p>
